  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of ZnCoN crystallizes in the trigonal space group R-3 (No. 143), with a unit cell of 36 atoms (Zn12Co12N12) distributed over four independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis shows Co and Zn centers each coordinated by three N neighbors at 1.93–2.09 Å, while N centers adopt two environments: one with six neighbors (3 Co, 3 Zn) and one with nine neighbors (6 Co, 3 Zn). Validated polyhedron-sharing relations reveal corner- and edge-sharing between 6-vertex N polyhedra, and corner-sharing between N and 9-vertex N polyhedra. The geometric neighbor graph forms a single 3-periodic component spanning all 36 sites.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
